      "_agent_risk": "## Risk Analysis — AUT-8428: Supplier GSTIN Column Missing on Filter Clear\n\n---\n\n### Risks\n\n- **[HIGH] `preparePanWisePayload()` returns null/undefined when all GSTINs cleared.** In `libs/helpers/src/lib/BusinessHelper.tsx:49-78`, when `inputOptions` is falsy (empty array or null after clearing), the function returns `inputOptions` as-is. There is **no fallback** to the current business unit. This causes `business_gstin: undefined` or `business_gstin: \"\"` to be sent to the API, which may return data without `stin`/`supplier_gstin` fields populated, making the column appear blank or get hidden.\n\n- **[HIGH] Two separate code paths affected — IMS AND GST Reports.** The \"Supplier GSTIN\" column exists in at least 4 places:\n  - IMS Inward (`apps/enterprise/src/app/IMS/ListView/columns.tsx:223-228`) — uses `stin` dataIndex\n  - IMS Outward (`apps/enterprise/src/app/IMS/Outward/columns.tsx:131-136`) — uses `supplier_gstin` dataIndex\n  - GSTR2B Supplier-Wise (`libs/entp/src/lib/reports/GstReport/ViewReport/GSTR2B/SupplierWiseDetail/columns.tsx`) — uses `ctin` dataIndex\n  - Column data helper (`libs/entp/src/lib/reports/GstReport/ViewReport/ColumnHelper/columnData.tsx`) — uses `supplier_gstin` group\n  \n  The fix must cover **all affected locations**, not just one.\n\n- **[HIGH] Inconsistent field names (`stin` vs `supplier_gstin` vs `ctin`) create confusion.** Different modules use different dataIndex keys for what appears to be the same concept. A fix applied to one field name may miss others.\n\n- **[MEDIUM] No explicit \"current business unit\" fallback logic anywhere in the filter chain.** The ticket says \"it should show the current business unit in case business unit filter is not selected,\" but neither `getFilteredData()` in `IMS/ListView/index.tsx:143-165` nor `IMS/Outward/index.tsx` implements this fallback. The Dashboard (`apps/enterprise/src/app/Dashboard/index.tsx:85-86`) initializes with ALL GSTINs but doesn't handle the \"cleared\" case either.\n\n- **[MEDIUM] `AppTreeSelect` allows clearing to empty state without guard.** The filter component in `IMS/ListView/FilterOptions.tsx:17-25` uses `AppTreeSelect` but has no `onChange` handler to prevent or intercept empty selection. The filter can reach a state the downstream code doesn't handle.\n\n- **[MEDIUM] Column visibility is stored in localStorage and may become stale.** `currentFields` is loaded from localStorage key `'ims'` (IMS ListView, lines 188-210). If the column list was saved without `stin`/`supplier_gstin` during a previous \"cleared\" session, it may persist incorrect visibility on subsequent loads even after the fix.\n\n- **[LOW] Backend API behavior when `business_gstin` is empty/null is undefined.** It's unclear whether the backend returns data with `stin`/`supplier_gstin` fields populated or omitted when no GSTIN filter is provided. The fix may need coordination with backend.\n\n- **[LOW] Regression risk to other filter consumers.** `preparePanWisePayload()` is used by 15+ components (Reports, Dashboard, IMS, etc.). Changing its behavior when input is empty could affect other screens that currently rely on the existing behavior.\n\n---\n\n### Suggestions\n\n- **[GAP]** The ticket says \"refer to SS 38\" but no screenshot is attached or referenced in the ticket context. It's **unclear which specific screen** (IMS Inward, IMS Outward, or GST Report GSTR2B) the bug was reported on. Clarify with QA which exact page/tab reproduces the issue.\n\n- **[GAP]** The acceptance criteria says \"show the current business unit\" — but `currentBusiness` / `activeGstin` is not passed into the filter or column components today. The source of \"current business unit\" (likely from user session/context) needs to be identified and threaded through.\n\n- **[GAP]** No API spec defines what the backend returns when `business_gstin` is empty. Does it return all data across GSTINs? Does it omit the `stin` field? Does it return an error? This must be verified before implementing the fix.\n\n- **[GAP]** The column visibility logic in `getInvIMSColumns()` does not receive filter state — it only receives `selectedCategory`. There's no mechanism today for the column generator to know whether GSTINs were selected or cleared, which means the column can't be conditionally shown/hidden based on filter state without a refactor.\n\n- **[RISK]** Modifying `preparePanWisePayload()` to return a default value when input is empty could break other consumers that intentionally pass empty to mean \"all\" or \"none.\" Each consumer should be audited.\n\n- **[RISK]** If the fix adds fallback logic only in IMS ListView but the bug also exists in IMS Outward and GSTR2B, the same defect will be reported again on those screens.\n\n- **[RISK]** localStorage-persisted column selections may cache the \"broken\" state. After fix, users who previously triggered the bug may still see the issue until they clear localStorage or reset column selection.\n\n- **[REC]** Explore the Dashboard's initialization pattern (`Dashboard/index.tsx:85-86`) which uses `getAllGstinList(panWiseBusinesses.map(item => item.value))` to default to all GSTINs. Apply the same pattern in `getFilteredData()` as a fallback when `business_gstin` is empty.\n\n- **[REC]** Check the `usePanWiseBusinesses()` hook and `useCurrentBusiness()` hook to find the current business unit GSTIN. Use it as the fallback value in `getFilteredData()` when `filterData.business_gstin` is empty/null.\n\n- **[REC]** Reuse the existing pattern from `IMS/ListView/index.tsx:167-183` where `initialFilterData` is set to `getTreeValues(panWiseBusinesses)`. The fix should ensure that when the user clears the filter and clicks apply, the same default is restored instead of sending empty.\n\n- **[REC]** After implementing the fix, verify column behavior in all 4 affected locations (IMS Inward, IMS Outward, GSTR2B supplier view, GST Report column helper). Use existing `defaultColumns` arrays as reference to ensure `stin`/`supplier_gstin`/`ctin` are always included.\n\n- **[REC]** Add a guard in the filter's `onFinish`/apply handler: if `business_gstin` is empty after user clears all, substitute the current business unit's GSTIN before calling the API. This is the minimal, targeted fix with lowest regression risk.",
      "_agent_requirements": "Error: Reached max turns (4)",
      "_agent_explorer": "Error: Reached max turns (10)",
      "_agent_analysis": "Error: Reached max turns (4)\n\nError: Reached max turns (10)\n\n## Risk Analysis — AUT-8428: Supplier GSTIN Column Missing on Filter Clear\n\n---\n\n### Risks\n\n- **[HIGH] `preparePanWisePayload()` returns null/undefined when all GSTINs cleared.** In `libs/helpers/src/lib/BusinessHelper.tsx:49-78`, when `inputOptions` is falsy (empty array or null after clearing), the function returns `inputOptions` as-is. There is **no fallback** to the current business unit. This causes `business_gstin: undefined` or `business_gstin: \"\"` to be sent to the API, which may return data without `stin`/`supplier_gstin` fields populated, making the column appear blank or get hidden.\n\n- **[HIGH] Two separate code paths affected — IMS AND GST Reports.** The \"Supplier GSTIN\" column exists in at least 4 places:\n  - IMS Inward (`apps/enterprise/src/app/IMS/ListView/columns.tsx:223-228`) — uses `stin` dataIndex\n  - IMS Outward (`apps/enterprise/src/app/IMS/Outward/columns.tsx:131-136`) — uses `supplier_gstin` dataIndex\n  - GSTR2B Supplier-Wise (`libs/entp/src/lib/reports/GstReport/ViewReport/GSTR2B/SupplierWiseDetail/columns.tsx`) — uses `ctin` dataIndex\n  - Column data helper (`libs/entp/src/lib/reports/GstReport/ViewReport/ColumnHelper/columnData.tsx`) — uses `supplier_gstin` group\n  \n  The fix must cover **all affected locations**, not just one.\n\n- **[HIGH] Inconsistent field names (`stin` vs `supplier_gstin` vs `ctin`) create confusion.** Different modules use different dataIndex keys for what appears to be the same concept. A fix applied to one field name may miss others.\n\n- **[MEDIUM] No explicit \"current business unit\" fallback logic anywhere in the filter chain.** The ticket says \"it should show the current business unit in case business unit filter is not selected,\" but neither `getFilteredData()` in `IMS/ListView/index.tsx:143-165` nor `IMS/Outward/index.tsx` implements this fallback. The Dashboard (`apps/enterprise/src/app/Dashboard/index.tsx:85-86`) initializes with ALL GSTINs but doesn't handle the \"cleared\" case either.\n\n- **[MEDIUM] `AppTreeSelect` allows clearing to empty state without guard.** The filter component in `IMS/ListView/FilterOptions.tsx:17-25` uses `AppTreeSelect` but has no `onChange` handler to prevent or intercept empty selection. The filter can reach a state the downstream code doesn't handle.\n\n- **[MEDIUM] Column visibility is stored in localStorage and may become stale.** `currentFields` is loaded from localStorage key `'ims'` (IMS ListView, lines 188-210). If the column list was saved without `stin`/`supplier_gstin` during a previous \"cleared\" session, it may persist incorrect visibility on subsequent loads even after the fix.\n\n- **[LOW] Backend API behavior when `business_gstin` is empty/null is undefined.** It's unclear whether the backend returns data with `stin`/`supplier_gstin` fields populated or omitted when no GSTIN filter is provided. The fix may need coordination with backend.\n\n- **[LOW] Regression risk to other filter consumers.** `preparePanWisePayload()` is used by 15+ components (Reports, Dashboard, IMS, etc.). Changing its behavior when input is empty could affect other screens that currently rely on the existing behavior.\n\n---\n\n### Suggestions\n\n- **[GAP]** The ticket says \"refer to SS 38\" but no screenshot is attached or referenced in the ticket context. It's **unclear which specific screen** (IMS Inward, IMS Outward, or GST Report GSTR2B) the bug was reported on. Clarify with QA which exact page/tab reproduces the issue.\n\n- **[GAP]** The acceptance criteria says \"show the current business unit\" — but `currentBusiness` / `activeGstin` is not passed into the filter or column components today. The source of \"current business unit\" (likely from user session/context) needs to be identified and threaded through.\n\n- **[GAP]** No API spec defines what the backend returns when `business_gstin` is empty. Does it return all data across GSTINs? Does it omit the `stin` field? Does it return an error? This must be verified before implementing the fix.\n\n- **[GAP]** The column visibility logic in `getInvIMSColumns()` does not receive filter state — it only receives `selectedCategory`. There's no mechanism today for the column generator to know whether GSTINs were selected or cleared, which means the column can't be conditionally shown/hidden based on filter state without a refactor.\n\n- **[RISK]** Modifying `preparePanWisePayload()` to return a default value when input is empty could break other consumers that intentionally pass empty to mean \"all\" or \"none.\" Each consumer should be audited.\n\n- **[RISK]** If the fix adds fallback logic only in IMS ListView but the bug also exists in IMS Outward and GSTR2B, the same defect will be reported again on those screens.\n\n- **[RISK]** localStorage-persisted column selections may cache the \"broken\" state. After fix, users who previously triggered the bug may still see the issue until they clear localStorage or reset column selection.\n\n- **[REC]** Explore the Dashboard's initialization pattern (`Dashboard/index.tsx:85-86`) which uses `getAllGstinList(panWiseBusinesses.map(item => item.value))` to default to all GSTINs. Apply the same pattern in `getFilteredData()` as a fallback when `business_gstin` is empty.\n\n- **[REC]** Check the `usePanWiseBusinesses()` hook and `useCurrentBusiness()` hook to find the current business unit GSTIN. Use it as the fallback value in `getFilteredData()` when `filterData.business_gstin` is empty/null.\n\n- **[REC]** Reuse the existing pattern from `IMS/ListView/index.tsx:167-183` where `initialFilterData` is set to `getTreeValues(panWiseBusinesses)`. The fix should ensure that when the user clears the filter and clicks apply, the same default is restored instead of sending empty.\n\n- **[REC]** After implementing the fix, verify column behavior in all 4 affected locations (IMS Inward, IMS Outward, GSTR2B supplier view, GST Report column helper). Use existing `defaultColumns` arrays as reference to ensure `stin`/`supplier_gstin`/`ctin` are always included.\n\n- **[REC]** Add a guard in the filter's `onFinish`/apply handler: if `business_gstin` is empty after user clears all, substitute the current business unit's GSTIN before calling the API. This is the minimal, targeted fix with lowest regression risk.",
